  "neighborhoods": "Northwest San Francisco, Pacific Heights",
  "description_text": "An exceptional Pacific Heights residence of striking presence, situated on the north side of a notably flat block of Pacific Avenue among some of San Francisco's finest private homes. Fully detached, with approximately 10,085 square feet, seven bedrooms, extraordinary principal rooms, panoramic Golden Gate Bridge and Bay views, and an expansive landscaped garden. The home's classical architecture is distinguished by a handsome brick faade and prominent rounded bay. Inside, a magnificent reception gallery with 10-foot ceilings opens to a grand staircase rising through a skylit hall to the uppermost floor. The sun-filled formal living room, with its beautiful marble fireplace, measures approximately 35 by 22 feet before extending into a rounded bay with a formal dining area. An extraordinary opportunity lies in two generously proportioned north-facing rooms overlooking the Golden Gate Bridge, Bay, and rear lawn. Originally configured as a formal dining room and adjoining study, these rooms could be transformed into an approximately 42-foot great room combining a new kitchen, family dining, and living spaces. Enlarged windows could further embrace the panoramic views, while the existing kitchen could become a separate chef's kitchen. The primary suite features a private lounge opening to a terrace with even more expansive views of the Golden Gate Bridge and Bay. Separate bathrooms, dressing areas, generous closets, and a study complete the suite. Two additional south-facing rooms on this level, currently used as a study and family room, could be transformed into guest bedrooms with ensuite baths. The uppermost floor includes five bedrooms and two baths, with opportunities to create beautiful living spaces that take advantage of the panoramic views. A magnificent, nearly level rear lawn is framed by mature landscaping and established hedges, offering generous space for outdoor living and recreation. The service level includes a staff bedroom and bath, wine cellar, mechanical room, two-car garage with interior access, and a large north-facing room with Bay views suited to a gym or recreation room. An elevator serves all four levels. A remarkable opportunity to bring the architectural distinction and scale of a great historic San Francisco residence into the 21st century.",
